11. Definitions.

  (a) "Authorised Deployment" means an instance of the protocol contracts
      deployed by the Licensor, or by another person with the Licensor's
      written authorisation, at the addresses the Licensor publishes, including
      in the SDK's address configuration, together with every contract created,
      directly or indirectly, by such an instance.

  (b) "Non-Production Use" means use for evaluation, development, testing,
      security research, audit or education that, if it runs on a network, runs
      only on a local, test or development network, does not create, record or
      transfer rights, obligations or value for any person, and does not
      provide the Software's functionality to third parties as a product or
      service. Any other use is "Production Use".

  (c) "Competing Product" means a product or service, whether or not offered
      for a fee, that provides functionality substantially similar to the
      Software or to a product or service that the Licensor or one of its
      affiliates provides using the Software, regardless of interface,
      platform, network or programming language. A product that provides its
      functionality through Authorised Deployments is not a Competing Product.

  (d) "You" means the person or entity agreeing to these terms, and "your
      company" means every organisation you work for and every organisation
      that controls, is controlled by, or is under common control with it.

  (e) An "affiliate" of the Licensor is any organisation that controls, is
      controlled by, or is under common control with it. Control means the
      power to direct an organisation's management and policies, by ownership,
      vote, contract or otherwise.

  (f) "Distribute" includes making the Software, or any part of it, available
      to third parties by any means.

  (g) "Licensor's Services" means the services the Licensor, or another person
      with the Licensor's written authorisation, operates using the Software,
